&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Software Engineer - Control Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Control Systems team translates customer intent into the configuration data that powers Fastly&#39;s edge. Because our services are central to how every product and feature reaches the edge, this role offers a unique opportunity to partner with internal teams across the organization to shape, scale, and secure the core Fastly experience that our customers rely on every day. As a Staff Software Engineer, you will join a talented group of engineers who solve complex problems in high-availability systems within a supportive environment where teammates genuinely enjoy working together. If you are a motivated engineer who thrives on solving interesting problems at scale while fostering a culture of high trust, mutual respect, and shared ownership, you’ll find a rewarding home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support, deploy, and share responsibility for large scale Perl production systems that store and ship configuration changes to thousands of nodes globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive architectural and operational improvements by evolving complex legacy systems into maintainable, performant Go microservices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership of engineering projects, coordinate with project stakeholders, and motivate progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across engineering teams to ensure our configuration systems meet the requirements for new features and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support other engineers, cultivating an environment of knowledge sharing, innovation, and teamwork within the engineering organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant domain-relevant engineering experience building highly reliable distributed systems. Most Staff Engineers at Fastly have at least 7 years of related experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid understanding of the Go programming language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic approach to legacy systems, including experience in or a willingness to learn Perl to support, troubleshoot, and enhance our core infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to drive and deliver complex projects that span multiple teams and require cross-organizational influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A communicative and empathetic teammate who works effectively in a remote environment and is comfortable with asynchronous workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An adaptable problem-solver who learns from mistakes, navigates ambiguity with ease, and balances short-term delivery with long-term quality through thoughtful tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’ll be super impressed if you have experience in any of these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background writing production-level code using the Perl programming language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerization systems and platforms such as Kubernetes and Docker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to monitoring solutions such as Prometheus and Grafana.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
